<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell seven points to 1,274.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell seven points to 1,274.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,274 today from 1,281 on April 24, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1340    12.169	  1329    12.063</p>
<p>   1a   1278  9681.000	  1302  9863.000</p>
<p>   2    1535    21.931	  1540    22.000</p>
<p>   2a   1470 12056.000	  1473 12081.000</p>
<p>   3    1362    12.539	  1370    12.638</p>
<p>   3a   1178  9300.000	  1205  9513.000</p>
